  "description": "<div style=\"font-family: Poppins;\"><div><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">• About our brand and products:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">The Putting Alley is a one-of-a-kind patented product that will develop a true precision putting stroke simply through repetition and guidance from you. &nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\"><br>• What makes us different:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">The Putting Alley is an updated version of \"putting on a yardstick\" that has been known to hone the putting face angle at impact. &nbsp;However, now the process is super simplified to using a single ball and rolling on extremely precise, level, different-width allies with auto ball return.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">• How affiliates can earn:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">Simply learn the benefits of The Alley and promote them to your golf students with suggestions of use. &nbsp;Encourage best grips and posture, proper swing path and games that might help the student golfer.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\"><br>• How to promote us:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">Trying to hone the face angle on a putting green is a waste of time., because of the excess number of variables in play: &nbsp;grass grain, length and growth; curvature of greens; the lumpy donut around the hole; different green speeds, and many others. &nbsp;In effect, greens can actually cause the stroke to become average (per Dave Pelz teaching).</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-size: 14px;font-weight: normal;\">So, use the Putting Alley away from the green - at home where many free time opportunities exist - to hone the stroke. &nbsp;Once the stroke is getting perfected then go out to the green and practice speed and break. &nbsp;Continue to come back to the Putting Alley to continue to keep building the stroke precision.&nbsp;</p></div></div>",
